    title: "Kushner says Israel is becoming a 'pariah' as his Board of Peace plans stall",
    summary: "Kushner says Israel is becoming a 'pariah' as his Board of Peace plans stall Israel is on track to become a “global pariah” over its genocide in the Gaza Strip, Jared Kushner, US President Donald Trump’s son-in-law and diplomatic envoy, said in an interview released on Monday. “Israel could rise from the tragedy of October 7, [and] be much more secure and much more integrated into the world, or they can go on the current trajectory, which is to trend toward global-pariah status,” Kushner said in an interview with New York Magazine. The remarks are notable given Kushner’s longtime advocacy for Israel and efforts to put it at the centre of a new regional security architecture in the Middle East. Kushner is a longtime family friend of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and created the controversial Board of Peace which was supposed to oversee Gaza’s reconstruction.  Peace plans stall US special envoy Jared Kushner pictured last week (Hannah McKay/AFP)",
    preview: "Kushner says Israel is becoming a 'pariah' as his Board of Peace plans stall Israel is on track to become a “global pariah” over its genocide in the Gaza Strip, Jared Kushner, US President Donald Trump’s son-in-law and diplomatic envoy, said in an interview released on Monday. “Israel could rise from the tragedy of October 7, [and] be much more secure and much more integrated into the world, or they can go on the current trajectory, which is to trend toward global-pariah status,” Kushner said in an interview with New York Magazine.",
    body: "Kushner says Israel is becoming a 'pariah' as his Board of Peace plans stall Israel is on track to become a “global pariah” over its genocide in the Gaza Strip, Jared Kushner, US President Donald Trump’s son-in-law and diplomatic envoy, said in an interview released on Monday. “Israel could rise from the tragedy of October 7, [and] be much more secure and much more integrated into the world, or they can go on the current trajectory, which is to trend toward global-pariah status,” Kushner said in an interview with New York Magazine.\n\nThe remarks are notable given Kushner’s longtime advocacy for Israel and efforts to put it at the centre of a new regional security architecture in the Middle East. Kushner is a longtime family friend of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and created the controversial Board of Peace which was supposed to oversee Gaza’s reconstruction. Peace plans stall US special envoy Jared Kushner pictured last week (Hannah McKay/AFP)",
