    title: "Who wins from Baghdad's move to clip Kurdish autonomy - the US or Iran?",
    summary: "Who wins from Baghdad's move to clip Kurdish autonomy - the US or Iran? Iraqi Prime Minister Ali al-Zaidi has said Baghdad will take over all of Kurdistan's border crossings and several oil fields that the autonomous region controls, in a move that was widely condemned by the region’s leaders as a step to clip their autonomy. Baghdad’s decision comes at a time of internal division in the Kurdistan Regional Government (KRG) and as the Middle East braces for a potential new US-Israeli attack on Iran. Under American pressure, Zaidi recently attempted to crack down on Kataib Hezbollah, a powerful Shia militia in Iraq aligned with Iran, which officials in Baghdad say has earned hundreds of millions of dollars from smuggling oil. Zaidi's spokesperson Sabah al-Numan said on Tuesday that, based on those findings, Baghad would take control of \"all border crossings in the Kurdistan Region\". e US or Iran? Iranian trucks waiting to cross back into Iran in the Penjwen district in Iraq's semi-autonomous Kurdistan Region in September 2026 (Safin Hamid/AFP)",
