    categories: ["conflitti"],
    title: "Is the war in the Middle East spilling into Europe?",
    summary: "Is the war in the Middle East spilling into Europe? From cyberattacks on fridges to threats against military bases hosting US forces, European authorities have accused Iran of planning attacks on their countries. Iran has rejected those accusations. Meanwhile, the war between Iran, the US and Israel has been in stalemate for months. And Iranian officials have threatened to bomb American bases in Europe should the US attack the country. So, what’s happening? Middle East Eye's Maya Saad takes a look.",
    preview: "Is the war in the Middle East spilling into Europe? From cyberattacks on fridges to threats against military bases hosting US forces, European authorities have accused Iran of planning attacks on their countries. Iran has rejected those accusations. Meanwhile, the war between Iran, the US and Israel has been in stalemate for months. And Iranian officials have threatened to bomb American bases in Europe should the US attack the country. So, what’s happening? Middle East Eye's Maya Saad takes a look.",
    body: "Is the war in the Middle East spilling into Europe? From cyberattacks on fridges to threats against military bases hosting US forces, European authorities have accused Iran of planning attacks on their countries. Iran has rejected those accusations. Meanwhile, the war between Iran, the US and Israel has been in stalemate for months. And Iranian officials have threatened to bomb American bases in Europe should the US attack the country.\n\nSo, what’s happening? Middle East Eye's Maya Saad takes a look.",
