    title: "Kushner says Israel is becoming a 'pariah' as his Board of Peace plans stall",
    summary: "Kushner says Israel is becoming a 'pariah' as his Board of Peace plans stall Submitted by MEE staff on Tue, 11/24/2026 - 18:33 US president's son-in-law has faced funding issues and delays in his attempt to reconstruct Gaza with Gulf cash US special envoy Jared Kushner pictured last week (Hannah McKay/AFP) Off Israel is on track to become a “global pariah” over its genocide in the Gaza Strip, Jared Kushner, US President Donald Trump’s son-in-law and diplomatic envoy, said in an interview released on Monday. “Israel could rise from the tragedy of October 7, [and] be much more secure and much more integrated into the world, or they can go on the current trajectory, which is to trend toward global-pariah status,” Kushner said in an interview with New York Magazine. The remarks are notable given Kushner’s longtime advocacy for Israel and efforts to put it at the centre of a new regional security architecture in the Middle East. Kushner is a longtime family friend of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and created the controversial Board of Peace which was supposed to oversee Gaza’s reconstruction. It is not clear what motivated Kushner’s comments, but his bid to be a Middle East peacemaker and builder has not held up, with Israel attacking the besieged enclave and much hyped-up reconstruction projects stalled. The enclave was pummelled by Israel in a genocide of Palestinians after the Hamas-led 7 October 2023 attack on southern Israel. More than 70,000 Palestinians were killed in the onslaught with 1,679 people killed in Israeli strikes since the October 2025 “ceasefire” Kushner helped broker was announced. The UN estimates it will cost $70bn to rebuild Gaza, but Kushner has struggled to launch even a small $2.45bn rebuilding project involving 66 projects across the enclave. Kushner blamed \"different delays on different things, for whatever reason\", during a presentation on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly in New York City in September. Israel kills UN worker and two others across Gaza as attacks on Palestinians continue  the Gaza Strip with a combination of Gulf financing, supranational advisers, some Palestinian technocrats and an outside security force. But the Gulf states have withheld funding and now face economic contractions because of the US-Israeli war on Iran. Middle East Eye revealed in May that Aryeh Lightstone, one of the key US officials overseeing the US’s post-war planning for Gaza, went to Saudi Arabia in the spring to lobby for funding but returned empty handed. The much discussed international stabilisation force has not entered the territory and the Palestinian technocrats supposed to run day-to-day affairs also remain in Cairo. The Times of Israel reported that “less than 2 percent” of the $17bn in pledges the Board of Peace was given have been met. In a sign of the board’s desperation, senior envoy Nickolay Mladenov travelled to Moscow on Monday and said Russia could contribute as a permanent member of the UN Security Council. Israel's genocide in Gaza News Post Date Override 0 Update Date Mon, 05/04/2020 - 21:19 Update Date Override 0",
