    body: "Taiwan’s voters seeking a bigger share of the spoils of the artificial intelligence-led boom will head to the polls on Saturday to choose more than 11,000 mayors and officials in local elections with global implications.\n\nThe results could reshape Taiwan’s political landscape ahead of the 2028 presidential ballot, determining whether President Lai Ching-te emerges strengthened at the midpoint of his first four-year term.\n\nLai’s Democratic Progressive Party, which favors self-determination for the island, is battling the China-friendly Kuomintang and its smaller ally, the Taiwan People’s Party. With neither the presidency nor legislature up for grabs, the focus is on grassroots issues like traffic and food safety, care for elders and children, and the cost of living. Yet the outcome could have far-reaching ramifications.",
