    summary: "Makoto Sakurai, who served on the BOJ's board from 2016 to 2021, isn't ruling out borrowing costs eventually rising above 2%, depending on inflation.",
    preview: "The Bank of Japan will likely raise its benchmark interest rate three more times to 2% through the middle of next year, taking it to a level not seen since 1993, according to a former BOJ board member. “The BOJ is probably thinking of raising the rate to 2%,” Makoto Sakurai, who served on the BOJ’s board from 2016 to 2021, said in an interview on Tuesday.",
    body: "The Bank of Japan will likely raise its benchmark interest rate three more times to 2% through the middle of next year, taking it to a level not seen since 1993, according to a former BOJ board member.\n\n“The BOJ is probably thinking of raising the rate to 2%,” Makoto Sakurai, who served on the BOJ’s board from 2016 to 2021, said in an interview on Tuesday. “Then they will take some time to see how things develop before deciding what to do next.”\n\nSakurai’s forecast is slightly above the median estimate of BOJ watchers for a so-called terminal rate of around 1.75%. He also said he isn’t ruling out borrowing costs eventually rising above 2%, depending on the inflation outlook.",
